# Forge

Read `docs/forge-principles.md` before product or UX changes. Do not alter the meaning of the原典.

- Judge features by whether they strengthen: 投稿 → 発見 → プレイ → フィードバック → 改善 → 再プレイ
- Do not change specs for implementation convenience
- Do not store shared production user data in localStorage (drafts/UI state only; Supabase for persistence)
- **GPT memo format is permanent** until owner explicitly requests a format change — always follow **`docs/chatgpt-summary-format.md`** (sole standard; do not revert to thinner/older format).
- On task completion **or any Forge status/deploy/verification reply**: update `docs/chatgpt-summary.md` per **`docs/chatgpt-summary-format.md`** (plain text, `■` headings, **thick not thin**: roadmap 60+ lines, impl 40+ lines, multi-line per section, owner decisions + reasons; **keep** なぜこの設計/他案不採用/In Out/リスク/オーナー確認; **add** `■ 今回変更した画面` when UI changed — screen name, URL, **画面位置**, before/after, player/dev perspective, verify steps; no Markdown tables/`#`/`---`/code fences), then **always** paste the **identical** content in one ```text block at the **end of the response** — owner uses Copy for ChatGPT; never skip unless user says メモ不要. Pre-send: summary updated + text block + **granularity check** (see AGENTS.md §GPT用メモ省略禁止).
- **`docs/chatgpt-handoff.md`**: update **only** on handoff triggers — major theme done, migration applied, **roadmap priority change**, or owner says 引継ぎ. New GPT thread: paste handoff once, then summary per task. See `docs/chatgpt-summary-format.md` §2ファイル運用.
- When a **design decision** is involved (DB, auth, notifications, permissions, storage, extensibility): add optional blocks per topic — `■ Cursorの推奨案` / `■ 推奨理由` / `■ 懸念点` (3–5 lines each). Not every task.
- Before **Run** on push/main/migration/DB deletes/prod deploy/billing-risk ops: **stop** and output the full **GPT判断用メモ** from `docs/gpt-run-decision-memo.md` (conclusion **[A]–[D]**; include Forge value / user impact / recovery difficulty). Owner×ChatGPT triage rules: **`docs/forge-triage-operations.md`**.

Full rules: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/forge-principles.md`, `docs/forge-triage-operations.md`.
